.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMM-CREATE-BACKUP 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emm-create-backup \- start a backup now instead of at the next scheduled time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B emm create-backup
[\fB\-\-full\fR | \fB\-\-config\-only\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a backup immediately - before an upgrade, say, or to check that
backups work at all. It is the nightly backup run early: written to the
same directory
.RI ( euclid.modules.emm.backup.directory ),
named the same way, encrypted when a passphrase is configured, and
pruned by the same retention afterwards. The caller must be
authenticated as an administrator; see
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1)
for how that's checked.
.PP
The command returns as soon as the backup has started, not when it has
finished: a backup that takes the bulk data reads every message and
object record there is, which can take far longer than a request should
stay open. The answer names the archive it will write.
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-backups (1)
shows it with
.I complete
set to
.I false
while it's being written, and
.I true
once it's done. If it fails, the reason is in EMM's log at error level.
.PP
Only one backup runs at a time. While one is being written, another
request fails with HTTP 409, and the nightly run is skipped with a
warning in the log.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-full
Also back up the bulk data - queue and topic messages, object records -
for this backup only. Ignored when a backup passphrase is set: an
encrypted backup is built in memory, and the bulk data is what doesn't
fit.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-only
Back up only the configuration (queues, topics, subscriptions, buckets,
users, roles, applications, servers, secrets), whatever
.I euclid.modules.emm.backup.full
says.
.PP
With neither,
.I euclid.modules.emm.backup.full
decides, as it does for the nightly backup.
.PP
Monitoring data
.RI ( emo )
is never part of a backup, and
.I ekm
is only included when a passphrase is set.
.SH OUTPUT
The JSON response is printed to standard output:
.RS
.TP
.I name ", " path
The archive the backup will write, and the same with its directory.
.TP
.I startedAt
When it started, in UTC.
.TP
.I full
Whether it takes the bulk data, after the options above and the
passphrase rule are applied.
.TP
.I encrypted
Whether it is sealed with the configured passphrase.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
once the backup has started,
.B 1
if it could not be started (a backup is already running, the caller is
not an administrator, or the request failed).
.SH EXAMPLES
Back up the configuration now:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm create-backup --config-only
.fi
.RE
.PP
Then check that it finished:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm list-backups
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-backups (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-export (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-import (1)
